<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Art (system: needs.beauty) - the one thing in this port's content that exists to be looked at.

    Why it ships with the beauty sampler rather than later. A beauty stat whose content has nothing positive
    in it averages zero or below everywhere, which makes the whole need a one-way misery gauge and, if filth
    had not landed first, a system that is dormant on arrival - the trap this project has now hit four times
    (citizen tiering, combat, the home area, and the beauty need itself). The fire lane's flammability and the
    filth lane's cleanliness both closed it the same way: ship the content that makes the number non-zero in
    the same change as the code that reads it. So: one sculpture, and a room with a few of them in it reads as
    pretty.

    Its own file, not an addition to any existing Buildings_*.xml, so nothing shared is touched (CLAUDE.md).

    Beauty 25, WorkToBuild, MaxHitPoints and the cost are SimWorld's own figures - RimWorld's real sculpture
    numbers were not sourceable here (its sculptures also carry a quality level this port does not have, which
    is most of where their beauty range comes from). BeautyTests pins the trend, not these: a room with art in
    it reads prettier than a bare one, and prettier still with more of it.

    The Blueprint_/Frame_ pair follows the hand-authored pattern every other buildable Def uses (see
    Buildings_BlueprintsAndFrames.xml's own remarks); without it a sculpture could be spawned but never built,
    which would be a smaller version of the same dormancy problem.
  -->

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>Sculpture</defName>
    <label>sculpture</label>
    <description>A carved figure, made to be looked at rather than used.</description>
    <category>Building</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Building.Building</thingClass>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <fillPercent>0.4</fillPercent>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>100</MaxHitPoints>
      <WorkToBuild>900</WorkToBuild>
      <Beauty>25</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <WoodLog>25</WoodLog>
    </costList>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>Blueprint_Sculpture</defName>
    <label>sculpture (blueprint)</label>
    <category>Blueprint</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Building.Blueprint</thingClass>
    <passability>Standable</passability>
    <entityToBuild>Sculpture</entityToBuild>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>Frame_Sculpture</defName>
    <label>sculpture (under construction)</label>
    <category>Frame</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Building.Frame</thingClass>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <fillPercent>0.4</fillPercent>
    <entityToBuild>Sculpture</entityToBuild>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
